# mockspace-refnames

The names of a mockspace reference, on the host's side of the `letkajenkka` standard. The standard owns the character set of a reference and leaves two things to its host: folding the host's own naming into that set, and the policy over what a parsed path may hold. Both are held here once, so every crate that reads or writes a reference folds and reads the same way. The character set itself is the standard's and is never restated here.

## What this crate provides

| Item | Role |
|---|---|
| `Folded` | A name as a reference writes it, folded from what a filesystem, a document or a config calls it: case lowered, each hyphen an underscore, and `LEAD` set before a name opening on a digit. It holds the name as given and never allocates; it shows itself only folded, through `Display`, and through comparison with a written name. |
| `Fold` | What a `Folded` holds, and so how it folds. Its two kinds are all there are. |
| `NameFold` | The kind of a name: a directory, a file up to its first dot, a heading, a row. A dot does not fold. |
| `ExtensionFold` | The kind of a file's extension, everything after its first dot, each further dot folded to an underscore: written only where two files differ by nothing else. |
| `FoldKind` | The seal on `Fold`, private to the crate, so no third kind can be added from outside. |
| `Extension` | A `Folded` of the extension kind. |
| `Fences` | The code fences of a document, inside which nothing is a reference. |
| `fold`, `extension`, `entry` | The only ways to make a `Folded`, each refusing a name that cannot fold into an identifier of the standard. |
| `CONFIG_FILES` | The files a config of lints is read from, in the order the loader tries them, shared by the loader and the migration that rewrites preset shorthands. |
| `LEAD`, `STAMP_DIGITS` | The letter set before a name that opens on a digit, and the digits of the `YYYYMMDDHHMM` stamp a research file or a round opens on. |

## What this crate does not do

- Parse a reference: that is `letkajenkka`'s.
- Resolve a reference to a file or a row: that is the registry's and the engine's.
- Allocate a folded name: a `Folded` borrows the name it was made from.
